lius.github.io/post/2024-06-05-numerical.mle/</link><pubDate>Sun, 05 Feb 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-06-05-numerical.mle/</guid><description>Numerical approaches to maximum likelihood estimation, covering the optimization methods and computational issues that come up in practice.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-06-05-numerical.mle/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Statistical Reliability</media:title></media:content><category>numerical-analysis</category><category>statistics</category><category>optimization</category></item><item><title>likelihood.model: Composable Likelihood Models in R</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-30-likelihood.model/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jun 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-30-likelihood.model/</guid><description>A generic R framework for composable likelihood models. Likelihoods are first-class objects that compose through independent contributions.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-30-likelihood.model/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Statistical Reliability</media:title></media:content><category>R</category><category>statistics</category><category>maximum likelihood</category><category>inference</category></item><item><title>Weibull Distributions: From Reliability Theory to My Own Survival Curve</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2022-04-weibull-survival-cancer/</link><pubDate>Mon, 18 Apr 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2022-04-weibull-survival-cancer/</guid><description>Weibull distributions model time-to-failure in reliability engineering and cancer survival. I study both professionally. One of them became personal.<