s</category><category>computational-statistics</category><category>monte-carlo</category></item><item><title>flexhaz: Specify the Hazard Function Directly</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-20-dfr.dist/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Aug 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-20-dfr.dist/</guid><description>An R package for specifying hazard functions directly instead of picking from a catalog of named distributions. You write the hazard. It handles the rest.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-20-dfr.dist/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Statistical Reliability</media:title></media:content><category>R</category><category>statistics</category><category>reliability</category><category>survival analysis</category><category>dynamic failure rate</category></item><item><title>algebraic.mle: MLEs as Algebraic Objects</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-15-algebraic.mle/</link><pubDate>Sat, 15 May 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-15-algebraic.mle/</guid><description>An R package that treats MLEs as algebraic objects. They carry Fisher information, compose through independent likelihoods, and propagate uncertainty correctly.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-05-15-algebraic.mle/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Statistical Reliability</media:title></media:content><category>R</category><category>statistics</category><category>maximum likelihood</category><category>algebra</category><category>Fisher information</category></item><item><title>Building R Packages for Statistical Inference</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2020-05-statistical-computing-r/</link><pubDate>Fri, 08 May 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid 